From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:24:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11123/11362] [outer-loop] The live self-discovery count rests
 on an argument, not a stamp

The new r11l level 2 moved the dashboard count from 4 to 5, so I checked
whether the credit is earned. The run artifact declares no solve_provenance,
no offline_reproduced and no reproduced_levels; all three are None.

Not a violation: the provenance contract triggers on offline_reproduced being
true, and the eval writes no such field, so nothing fires and the letter holds.
The credit instead rests on a structural argument stated in
generalization_levels(), that the eval is adapter-free by construction. That
argument is sound and the function is careful elsewhere, unioning batches
rather than taking freshest-wins and refusing to pool explorer with e3.

The gap is that the argument lives in one consumer. The second source in that
same function demands an explicit stamp and would credit these runs zero, and
any other reader sees None. Same shape as the engine-shape split recorded an
hour ago: a contract that stops at the producer's edge, with each consumer
compensating differently.

Filed as an operator decision rather than stamped here. One line would fix it,
but which artifact is the canonical provenance source is a contract choice and
not mine to settle.

